cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GEML in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "GEML: Graph Learning over a Single-Operator Representation of Mathematics"
abstract: >-
  GEML is a controlled representation study asking whether collapsing every
  elementary math operator into the single primitive eml(x, y) = exp(x) - ln(y)
  helps graph neural networks learn symbolic reasoning, given that the reduction
  inflates tree size. It is a clean-room production rebuild with preregistered
  gates, published null results, and one published gate failure. Prepared for
  submission to MathNLP 2026.
type: software
